{"body":{"text":["That a card is an anchor to the page's address the author holds wrong: \"yes the card being a link is wrong, a crd is just a card, navigation is external to what ever system builds it, our system is at the core nvaigation agnostic, the reader is one first example\" (23/21; 23/7). An href may still live in a Link component of the pilot's, tied to the reader (23/9). A URL and the reader's collation are the same thing to him, the URL \"just a state mechanism\" (23/29). *The card no link, settled, 23/21.*"]},"id":"1M88XH3QXW8P000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["How a press on a holon reaches what navigates is open. Readers in a split pane may not use the URL, or use different q's, and since the layout is a holarchy of locations, clickability could be at that level (23/19). A program for navigation, which he first called \"more of a side effect to me\" (23/15), is \"One clear way\", though how it reaches everything clickable is \"still a mystery\" (23/19). Prop drilling, a component catching clicks bubbling from nodes others drew, which he holds already settled as an antipattern, and proposing by an argument's position were let go (23/11, 23/13, 23/17); an offer from the root he doubts: \"it doesnt feel right\" (23/17). *Open: the thread Navigation outside what draws.*"]},"id":"1M88XH3QXW8P001","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Glass matches by type, never by order: \"we dont work with arguments in their order, only thourgh type matching it is a set not a list of arguments\" (23/17). So io.propose, which names what it changes by its index among what a component was given, owes a change. *Open: the thread Propose by type, not position.*"]},"id":"1M88XH3QXW8P002","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Where a component in code draws a holon in its own markup, as Value draws a card, the chassis cannot know it; layout as data hides nothing: \"a brief should be made by Holons itself. That's a problem with components as code. Now maybe components as code should have a way to declare what something is, so that it is available. But with layout as data, that's not a problem.\" (23/33). *Open: the thread Holons drawn inside components in code.*"]},"id":"1M88XH3QXW8P003","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Gestures are to be reserved at the root, which may \"set the rules of the game\" (23/27), as OpenLight's input floor reserved its own, and everything else is to be the components': \"at the root, reserve gestures, etc. Otherwise, it's for the components\" (23/29). Unlike the bubbling let go above, a component catching what others drew, input is to propagate up the holarchy until something captures it: \"user input propagating until captures is something we need\" (23/23), the same movements expected in a Rust app as on the web (23/25). Whether the propagating is ever stopped he does not know (23/27); of a button, \"pressing a button is pressing a button. Nothing's to be propagated there, I think\", though \"I can't say for sure that that's a golden rule\" (23/31). *Leaning, 23/23 to 23/29; open: the thread Input reserved at the root, propagated until captured.*"]},"id":"1M88XH3QXW8P004","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Right-click is so reserved for the context menu, which is given where it was pressed in the holarchy and does the rest by matching: \"It's all just pure matching\" (23/29). Perhaps each level up the tree shows as a label with its actions, global actions at the bottom (23/29). *Leaning, 23/29; open: the thread The context menu as matching over the holarchy.*"]},"id":"1M88XH3QXW8P005","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Above the content an overlay layer is to stand, the completion menu and the context menu its first: \"So that should be rendered in an overlay. And if we right-click on something, that's also an overlay.\" (23/27); \"I think we should do layers and the overlay system\" (23/29). He wants it scrutinised, \"I'd appreciate agents try to say it's not the right idea\" (23/29), and holds the agents' completion as the input's own popover \"the absolute opposite of what's been drawn\" (23/31). *Leaning, 23/27 and 23/29; open: the thread Layers and overlays.*"]},"id":"1M88XH3QXW8P006","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Chrome is no component's to implement, and whose it is is unknown: the parent giving the card and background \"seemed smart, seemed sane\" to him, though nesting troubles it and \"I can't quite grasp it yet\" (23/29); a focus ring is chrome too (23/31), and in OpenLight's reader selections in a collation \"maybe have different colors\" (23/27). *Open: the thread Chrome around nested components.*"]},"id":"1M88XH3QXW8P007","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Chassis of many kinds are to nest, DOM and canvas, a canvas perhaps mounting a visualization as a component taking a particular kind of data (23/29); and node-based views of holarchies, the interface's own above all, are wanted soon, seeing the layout as nodes a global action (23/27). *Open: the thread Chassis of many kinds, nested.*"]},"id":"1M88XH3QXW8P008","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Keys and accessibility are the system's to define, their data probably shipped with the field; what implements them \"might be up to the chassis, or might be a decoupled piece from the chassis. I don't know exactly\" (23/29), and \"I don't know if ARIA roles are enough\" (23/31). *Open: the thread Accessibility and keys defined by the system.*"]},"id":"1M88XH3QXW8P009","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Agents briefed narrowly fail that freedom. In the twenty-third session four were sent with one brief of the session's own framing, each started from a topic; the author did not know how informed they were and trusted the process little: \"this wasn't a particularly intelligent way of running agents either\" (23/31). The session conceded they argued its framing, one read Knowledge only in part, none had the conversation, and their agreement was one opinion counted four times (23/32). Perhaps, he said, \"running sub-agents, they'll have to bootstrap themselves properly\", and \"they all ought to explore without constraints, and they all ought to have a certain culture of exploration, of critique, and digestion\" (23/35). Whether agents sent alike all do the same, or spread by chance, he asks; steering them or siloing them by topic \"doesn't quite resonate\" with him, and their first talking among themselves he has not tried and doubts; \"So maybe we send off 3 just completely free to explore everything within there\" (23/35). *Open: the thread Free agents and their orchestration.*"]},"id":"1M88XH3QXW8P00A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}